From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitriy <noc@pimk.in>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:37:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: apple: Do not start the NHI without its
 DART

The NHI and its DART are both children of the ACIO and are created
together when the router starts. The DART normally binds first, and the
driver core defers the NHI until it has. Once the core has stopped
waiting for missing suppliers, though (for example, the DART driver is a
module that is not loaded yet when a cable is plugged in), the NHI
probes without an IOMMU and would hand the hardware physical ring
addresses.

Refuse to probe an NHI that has iommus but is not attached to an IOMMU
domain. Report it through the boot status as well, so that the ACIO
fails this start right away with -EPROBE_DEFER instead of waiting for
the 10 s NHI boot timeout; the next connection retries.

Signed-off-by: Dmitriy <noc@pimk.in>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit f6ba35b02115a9a41b0eb647b8c2f10b2632cf5e)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c
index cd6b351880..8bd53321be 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c
@@ -83,6 +83,7 @@
 #include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/io.h>
+#include <linux/iommu.h>
 #include <linux/iopoll.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/mutex.h>
@@ -2094,6 +2095,20 @@ static int apple_nhi_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		goto err;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The rings must never run untranslated. The DART is populated with
+	 * the NHI, so it is normally bound first; but once the driver core
+	 * has stopped waiting for missing suppliers (DART driver not loaded
+	 * yet), the NHI would probe without its IOMMU. Defer, and fail the
+	 * ACIO start now instead of letting it wait for the NHI to time out.
+	 */
+	if (of_property_present(pdev->dev.of_node, "iommus") &&
+	    !device_iommu_mapped(&pdev->dev)) {
+		dev_warn(&pdev->dev, "DART not bound yet, not starting the NHI\n");
+		ret = -EPROBE_DEFER;
+		goto err;
+	}
+
 	anhi = devm_kzalloc(&pdev->dev, sizeof(*anhi), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!anhi) {
 		ret = -ENOMEM;
